   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "For each ordered pair, decide:\n<ol type=\"I\">\n<li>Is the ordered pair a solution to the equation?</li>\n<li>Is the point on the line in the graph shown?</li>\n</ol>\n<span data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 2\">y = \\frac{1}{3}x + 2</span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"{\\text{A: }}(0, - 3)\\quad \\quad {\\text{B: }}( - 3,1);\\quad \\quad {\\text{C: }}( - 2, - 4);\\quad \\quad {\\text{D: }}(0,2)\">{\\text{A: }}(0, - 3)\\quad \\quad {\\text{B: }}( - 3,1);\\quad C:( - 2, - 4);\\quad D:(0,2)</span>\n\n<img src=\"exercises/media/6fd6085131e4722e.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on a coordinate plane. The horizontal and vertical axes range from negative 10 to 9, in increments of 1. The line passes through the points, (negative 6, 0), (0, 2), and (6, 4).\">\n",
